IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XII -- Shareholders: meetings (ss 132 to 136).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. A "prescribed period" is not
-- among the sources (the regulations): where the text says a thing must be done "within the prescribed
-- period", the rule takes a plain yes-or-no input "within the prescribed period", because the text does
-- not say whether the period is before or after the event, or one limit or two. A rule the by-laws or
-- articles may vary has an input saying whether they do, and, if they do, whether what they require is
-- met. Dates: Part XII holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XII -- Shareholders: meetings (ss 132 to 136)`

§§ `s 132 -- place of meetings, and meetings by electronic means`

-- (1) A meeting is held at the place within Canada that the by-laws provide; if they provide none, at the
-- place within Canada that the directors determine. The relation: the shareholders are owed a meeting
-- at a lawful place; the corporation (its directors) owes it.
-- src:1628 | 132 (1) Meetings of shareholders of a corporation shall be held at the place within Canada provided in the by-laws or, in the absence of such provision, at the place within Canada that the directors determine.
@ref CBCA s 132(1) (src:1628)
GIVEN `the place is within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws provide a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is the one the by-laws provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is the one the directors determine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the place of the meeting complies with s 132(1)` MEANS
        `the place is within Canada`
    AND (IF `the by-laws provide a place`
         THEN `the place is the one the by-laws provide`
         ELSE `the place is the one the directors determine`)

-- (2) Despite (1), a meeting may be held at a place outside Canada if the place is specified in the
-- articles or all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree to it.
-- src:1630 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a meeting of shareholders of a corporation may be held at a place outside Canada if the place is specified in the articles or all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that the meeting is to be held at that place.
@ref CBCA s 132(2) (src:1630)
GIVEN `the place is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is specified in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that the meeting is to be held at that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a meeting may be held outside Canada within s 132(2)` MEANS
        `the place is outside Canada`
    AND (    `the place is specified in the articles`
         OR  `all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that the meeting is to be held at that place`)

-- (3) A shareholder who attends a meeting held outside Canada is deemed to have agreed to its being held
-- there, except when the shareholder attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of
-- any business on the ground that the meeting is not lawfully held.
-- src:1632 | (3) A shareholder who attends a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada is deemed to have agreed to it being held outside Canada except when the shareholder attends the meeting for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held.
@ref CBCA s 132(3) (src:1632)
GIVEN `the shareholder attends a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder is deemed to have agreed to the meeting being held outside Canada within s 132(3)` MEANS
        `the shareholder attends a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada`
    AND (NOT `the shareholder attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held`)

-- (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any person entitled to attend may participate, in accordance with
-- the regulations (if any), by a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all
-- participants to communicate adequately, if the corporation makes such a facility available. A person
-- so participating is deemed present. If the by-laws otherwise provide, this default does not apply.
-- src:1634 | (4) Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any person entitled to attend a meeting of shareholders may participate in the meeting, in accordance with the regulations, if any, by means of a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting, if the corporation makes available such a communication facility. A person participating in a meeting by such means is deemed for the purposes of this Act to be present at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 132(4) (src:1634)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to attend the meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation makes a communication facility available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may participate by electronic means within s 132(4)` MEANS
        `the person is entitled to attend the meeting of shareholders`
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)
    AND `the corporation makes a communication facility available`
    AND `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting`
    AND `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any`

@ref CBCA s 132(4) (src:1634)
GIVEN `the person participates in the meeting by means of a communication facility under subsection 132(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person participating by electronic means is present at the meeting within s 132(4)` MEANS
    `the person participates in the meeting by means of a communication facility under subsection 132(4)`

-- (5) If the directors or the shareholders call a meeting pursuant to the Act, they may determine that it be
-- held entirely by electronic means (in accordance with the regulations, if any, and with a facility that
-- permits all participants to communicate adequately), if the by-laws so provide.
-- src:1636 | (5) If the directors or the shareholders of a corporation call a meeting of shareholders pursuant to this Act, those directors or shareholders, as the case may be, may determine that the meeting shall be held, in accordance with the regulations, if any, entirely by means of a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting, if the by-laws so provide.
@ref CBCA s 132(5) (src:1636)
GIVEN `the directors or the shareholders call the meeting pursuant to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the by-laws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the callers may determine that the meeting is held entirely by electronic means within s 132(5)` MEANS
        `the directors or the shareholders call the meeting pursuant to the Act`
    AND `the by-laws so provide`
    AND `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting`
    AND `the meeting is held in accordance with the regulations, if any`

§§ `s 133 -- calling meetings`

-- (1) The directors shall call an annual meeting (a) not later than eighteen months after the corporation
-- comes into existence; and (b) subsequently, not later than fifteen months after holding the last preceding
-- annual meeting but no later than six months after the end of the corporation's preceding financial year.
-- The text says CALL, not hold; the rules follow the text (fork F-133-call). The last day of a period counted
-- from a day is the keel's (fork F1): the start day is day 0, and the last day is in time.
-- The relation: the shareholders are owed an annual meeting; the directors owe it.
-- src:1638 | 133 (1) The directors of a corporation shall call an annual meeting of shareholders
-- src:1639 | (a) not later than eighteen months after the corporation comes into existence; and
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(a) (src:1638-1639)
`the eighteen months of s 133(1)(a)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 18, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

@ref CBCA s 133(1)(a) (src:1639)
GIVEN `the date the corporation comes into existence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to call the first annual meeting within s 133(1)(a)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the eighteen months of s 133(1)(a)` `counted from` `the date the corporation comes into existence`

@ref CBCA s 133(1)(a) (src:1639)
GIVEN `the date the corporation comes into existence` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors call the annual meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first annual meeting is called in time within s 133(1)(a)` MEANS
    `the date the directors call the annual meeting` AT MOST (`the last day to call the first annual meeting within s 133(1)(a)` `the date the corporation comes into existence`)

-- src:1640 | (b) subsequently, not later than fifteen months after holding the last preceding annual meeting but no later than six months after the end of the corporation’s preceding financial year.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b) (src:1640)
`the fifteen months of s 133(1)(b)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b) (src:1640)
`the six months of s 133(1)(b)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

-- Both limits apply ("but"): the meeting must be called by the EARLIER of fifteen months after the last
-- annual meeting and six months after the end of the preceding financial year.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b) (src:1640)
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to call a subsequent annual meeting within s 133(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of` `the fifteen months of s 133(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` AT MOST (`the last day of` `the six months of s 133(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`)
    THEN `the last day of` `the fifteen months of s 133(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held`
    ELSE `the last day of` `the six months of s 133(1)(b)` `counted from` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`

@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b) (src:1640)
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` IS A DATE
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors call the annual meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a subsequent annual meeting is called in time within s 133(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the date the directors call the annual meeting` AT MOST (`the last day to call a subsequent annual meeting within s 133(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`)

-- (2) The directors may call a special meeting at any time: no time limit, no condition.
-- src:1642 | (2) The directors of a corporation may at any time call a special meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 133(2) (src:1642)
GIVEN `the persons calling the meeting are the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may call a special meeting at any time within s 133(2)` MEANS
    `the persons calling the meeting are the directors of the corporation`

-- (3) Despite (1), the corporation may apply to the court for an order extending the time for calling an
-- annual meeting. Whether the court makes the order is its discretion and is not decided here.
-- src:1644 | (3) Despite subsection (1), the corporation may apply to the court for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 133(3) (src:1644)
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to the court to extend the time for calling an annual meeting within s 133(3)` MEANS
        `the applicant is the corporation`
    AND `the application is for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting`

§§ `s 134 -- fixing a record date`

-- (1) The directors may, within the prescribed period, fix in advance a date as the record date for
-- determining the shareholders entitled to receive a dividend, to participate in a liquidation distribution,
-- to receive notice of a meeting, to vote at a meeting, or "for any other purpose" (paragraph (e) leaves no
-- purpose out). The prescribed period is a yes-or-no input.
-- src:1646 | 134 (1) The directors may, within the prescribed period, fix in advance a date as the record date for the purpose of determining shareholders
-- src:1647 | (a) entitled to receive payment of a dividend;
-- src:1648 | (b) entitled to participate in a liquidation distribution;
-- src:1649 | (c) entitled to receive notice of a meeting of shareholders;
-- src:1650 | (d) entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders; or
-- src:1651 | (e) for any other purpose.
@ref CBCA s 134(1) (src:1646-1651)
GIVEN `the persons fixing the date are the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date is fixed in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date is fixed within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may fix a record date within s 134(1)` MEANS
        `the persons fixing the date are the directors`
    AND `the date is fixed in advance`
    AND `the date is fixed within the prescribed period`

-- (2) If no record date is fixed: (a) for notice of a meeting, the close of business on the day immediately
-- preceding the day on which the notice is given or, if no notice is given, the day on which the meeting is held;
-- (b) for any purpose other than notice or voting, the close of business on the day on which the directors pass
-- the resolution relating to it. The date is the day; "close of business" is the time of that day.
-- src:1654 | (a) the record date for the determination of shareholders entitled to receive notice of a meeting of shareholders shall be
-- src:1655 | (i) at the close of business on the day immediately preceding the day on which the notice is given, or
-- src:1656 | (ii) if no notice is given, the day on which the meeting is held; and
@ref CBCA s 134(2)(a) (src:1654-1656)
GIVEN `the date notice of the meeting is given, if notice is given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the meeting is held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the record date for notice of a meeting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date notice of the meeting is given, if notice is given`
    WHEN JUST given THEN given MINUS 1
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the meeting is held`

-- src:1657 | (b) the record date for the determination of shareholders for any purpose other than to establish a shareholder’s right to receive notice of a meeting or to vote shall be at the close of business on the day on which the directors pass the resolution relating thereto.
@ref CBCA s 134(2)(b) (src:1657)
GIVEN `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the record date for a purpose other than notice or voting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(b)` MEANS
    `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose`

-- The default record date for each purpose. For voting the text gives none: (a) is for notice and (b) is
-- expressly "any purpose other than ... to receive notice of a meeting or to vote". NOTHING is the
-- explicit answer "not covered by the text" (fork F-134-vote).
-- src:1652 | No record date fixed
-- src:1653 | (2) If no record date is fixed,
@ref CBCA s 134(2) (src:1652-1657)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose of a record date under s 134(1)`
      `the date notice of the meeting is given, if notice is given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the record date when none is fixed within s 134(2)` purpose `the date notice of the meeting is given, if notice is given` `the date the meeting is held` `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `a record date for receiving payment of a dividend` THEN JUST (`the record date for a purpose other than notice or voting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(b)` `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose`)
    WHEN `a record date for participating in a liquidation distribution` THEN JUST (`the record date for a purpose other than notice or voting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(b)` `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose`)
    WHEN `a record date for receiving notice of a meeting of shareholders` THEN JUST (`the record date for notice of a meeting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(a)` `the date notice of the meeting is given, if notice is given` `the date the meeting is held`)
    WHEN `a record date for voting at a meeting of shareholders` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a record date for any other purpose` THEN JUST (`the record date for a purpose other than notice or voting when none is fixed within s 134(2)(b)` `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose`)

-- (3) If a record date is fixed, notice of it must be given within the prescribed period, unless every holder
-- of a share of the class or series affected whose name is in the securities register at the close of business on
-- the day the directors fix the record date waives notice in writing; the notice is (a) an advertisement in a
-- newspaper published or distributed in the place of the registered office and in each place in Canada where the
-- corporation has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded, and (b) written notice to
-- each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares are listed for trading: both ("and"). The relation: those
-- holders are owed the notice; the corporation owes it.
-- src:1658 | When record date fixed
-- src:1659 | (3) If a record date is fixed, unless notice of the record date is waived in writing by every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is set out in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the record date, notice of the record date must be given within the prescribed period
-- src:1660 | (a) by advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded; and
-- src:1661 | (b) by written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares of the corporation are listed for trading.
@ref CBCA s 134(3) (src:1658-1661)
GIVEN `a record date is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is set out in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the record date has waived notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the record date must be given within s 134(3)` MEANS
        `a record date is fixed`
    AND (NOT `every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is set out in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the record date has waived notice in writing`)

@ref CBCA s 134(3) (src:1658-1661)
GIVEN `the notice is given within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares of the corporation are listed for trading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the record date is given as s 134(3) requires within s 134(3)` MEANS
        `the notice is given within the prescribed period`
    AND `there is an advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded`
    AND `there is written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares of the corporation are listed for trading`

§§ `s 135 -- notice of a meeting`

-- (1) Notice of the time and place of a meeting shall be sent within the prescribed period to (a) each
-- shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting, (b) each director and (c) the auditor. The relation: those three are
-- owed the notice; the corporation owes it. (1.1) A corporation that is not a distributing corporation may send
-- the notice within a shorter period if the articles or by-laws so specify.
-- src:1664 | 135 (1) Notice of the time and place of a meeting of shareholders shall be sent within the prescribed period to
-- src:1665 | (a) each shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting;
-- src:1666 | (b) each director; and
-- src:1667 | (c) the auditor of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 135(1) (src:1664-1667)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the meeting is owed to a person within s 135(1)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting`
    OR  `the person is a director`
    OR  `the person is the auditor of the corporation`

-- src:1669 | (1.1) In the case of a corporation that is not a distributing corporation, the notice may be sent within a shorter period if so specified in the articles or by-laws.
@ref CBCA s 135(1.1) (src:1669)
GIVEN `the notice was sent within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles or by-laws specify a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was sent within the shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting was sent in time within s 135(1) and (1.1)` MEANS
        `the notice was sent within the prescribed period`
    OR  (    (NOT `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)
         AND `the articles or by-laws specify a shorter period`
         AND `the notice was sent within the shorter period`)

-- (2) A notice is not required to be sent to a shareholder who was not registered on the records of the
-- corporation or its transfer agent on the record date determined under 134(1)(c) or 134(2); but failure to
-- receive a notice does not deprive a shareholder of the right to vote at the meeting.
-- src:1671 | (2) A notice of a meeting is not required to be sent to shareholders who were not registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date determined under paragraph 134(1)(c) or subsection 134(2), but failure to receive a notice does not deprive a shareholder of the right to vote at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 135(2) (src:1671)
GIVEN `the shareholder was registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice need not be sent to the shareholder within s 135(2)` MEANS
    (NOT `the shareholder was registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date`)

@ref CBCA s 135(2) (src:1671)
GIVEN `the shareholder is entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder keeps the right to vote without having received notice within s 135(2)` MEANS
    `the shareholder is entitled to vote at the meeting`

-- (3), (4) Adjournment. The days are the aggregate of the adjournments (fork F-135-adjourn). Adjourned for
-- LESS THAN thirty days: notice other than the announcement at the earliest meeting adjourned is not necessary,
-- unless the by-laws otherwise provide. Adjourned for THIRTY DAYS OR MORE: notice as for an original meeting;
-- and subsection 149(1) (the form of proxy) applies only if the aggregate is MORE THAN ninety days.
-- src:1673 | (3) If a meeting of shareholders is adjourned for less than thirty days it is not necessary, unless the by-laws otherwise provide, to give notice of the adjourned meeting, other than by announcement at the earliest meeting that is adjourned.
@ref CBCA s 135(3) (src:1673)
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the adjourned meeting other than by announcement is unnecessary within s 135(3)` MEANS
        `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` LESS THAN 30
    AND (NOT `the by-laws otherwise provide`)

-- src:1675 | (4) If a meeting of shareholders is adjourned by one or more adjournments for an aggregate of thirty days or more, notice of the adjourned meeting shall be given as for an original meeting but, unless the meeting is adjourned by one or more adjournments for an aggregate of more than ninety days, subsection 149(1) does not apply.
@ref CBCA s 135(4) (src:1675)
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`notice of the adjourned meeting is required as for an original meeting within s 135(4)` MEANS
    `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` AT LEAST 30

@ref CBCA s 135(4) (src:1675)
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsection 149(1) applies to the adjourned meeting within s 135(4)` MEANS
        `notice of the adjourned meeting is required as for an original meeting within s 135(4)` `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate`
    AND `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` GREATER THAN 90

-- (5) All business at a special meeting, and all business at an annual meeting except the consideration of the
-- financial statements, the auditor's report, the election of directors and the re-appointment of the incumbent
-- auditor, is deemed special business.
-- src:1677 | (5) All business transacted at a special meeting of shareholders and all business transacted at an annual meeting of shareholders, except consideration of the financial statements, auditor’s report, election of directors and re-appointment of the incumbent auditor, is deemed to be special business.
@ref CBCA s 135(5) (src:1677)
GIVEN `the meeting is a special meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is the consideration of the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is the consideration of the auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is the election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is the re-appointment of the incumbent auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the business is deemed to be special business within s 135(5)` MEANS
        `the meeting is a special meeting of shareholders`
    OR  (NOT (    `the business is the consideration of the financial statements`
              OR  `the business is the consideration of the auditor's report`
              OR  `the business is the election of directors`
              OR  `the business is the re-appointment of the incumbent auditor`))

-- (6) A notice of a meeting at which special business is to be transacted shall state (a) the nature of that
-- business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it, and (b) the text of
-- any special resolution to be submitted. "Sufficient detail" is a judgment taken as the input.
-- src:1679 | (6) Notice of a meeting of shareholders at which special business is to be transacted shall state
-- src:1680 | (a) the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment thereon; and
-- src:1681 | (b) the text of any special resolution to be submitted to the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 135(6) (src:1679-1681)
GIVEN `special business is to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a special resolution is to be submitted to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the text of the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting has the content s 135(6) requires within s 135(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `special business is to be transacted at the meeting`)
    OR  (    `the notice states the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it`
         AND (    (NOT `a special resolution is to be submitted to the meeting`)
              OR  `the notice states the text of the special resolution`))

§§ `s 136 -- waiver of notice`

-- A shareholder or any other person entitled to attend a meeting may in any manner waive notice of it, and
-- their attendance is a waiver of notice, except where they attend for the express purpose of objecting to the
-- transaction of any business on the ground that the meeting is not lawfully called.
-- src:1683 | 136 A shareholder or any other person entitled to attend a meeting of shareholders may in any manner waive notice of a meeting of shareholders, and their attendance at a meeting of shareholders is a waiver of notice of the meeting, except where they attend a meeting for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called.
@ref CBCA s 136 (src:1683)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may waive notice of the meeting within s 136` MEANS
    `the person is a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting`

@ref CBCA s 136 (src:1683)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`attendance is a waiver of notice within s 136` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting`
    AND `the person attends the meeting`
    AND (NOT `the person attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called`)
